3"} "20 kilometres, Men"]] [:script {} "$('#same_games_select').change(function(){location.href='/results/' + $('#same_games_select').val();})"]] " | " [:form {:class "form-inline form-inline-header"} [:select {:name "id", :id "other_games_select", :class "form-control"} [:option {:value ""} "In other Games"] "\n" [:option {:value "1518"} "1968"] "\n" [:option {:value "1523"} "1972"] "\n" [:option {:value "1528"} "1976"] "\n" [:option {:value "1540"} "1984"] "\n" [:option {:value "1546"} "1988"] "\n" [:option {:value "1552"} "1992"] "\n" [:option {:value "1563"} "1994"] "\n" [:option {:value "1575"} "1998"] "\n" [:option {:value "1588"} "2002"] "\n" [:option {:value "1603"} "2006"] "\n" [:option {:value "923486"} "2010"] "\n" [:option {:value "350026"} "2014"] "\n" [:option {:value "9000224"} "2018"] "\n" [:option {:value "19019634"} "2022"] "\n" [:option {:value "15000034"} "2026"]] [:script {} "$('#other_games_select').change(function(){location.href='/results/' + $('#other_games_select').val();})"]] " | " [:a {:href "/event_names/132"} "Event type"]] [:h1 {:class "event_title"} "4 × 7.5 kilometres Relay, Men" [:small {}]] [:table {:class "biodata"} [:tbody {} [:tr {} [:th {} "Date"] [:td {} "22 February 1980 — 9:00"]] [:tr {} [:th {} "Status"] [:td {} "Olympic"]] [:tr {} [:th {} "Location"] [:td {} [:a {:href "/venues/74"} "Mt. Van Hoevenberg Recreation Area, Lake Placid"]]] [:tr {} [:th {} "Participants"] [:td {} [:a {:href "/events/1534"} "60 from 15 countries"]]] [:tr {} [:th {} "Format"] [:td {:colspan "2"} "Eight shots for each group of five targets. Penalty loop (150 metres) skied for each missed target."]] [:tr {} [:th {:valign "top"} "Details"] [:td {} "Course Length: ?" [:br {}] "Height Differential: 42 m" [:br {}] "Maximum Climb: 33 m" [:br {}] "Shooting 1: Prone at 2.5 km, 50 m range" [:br {}] "Shooting 2: Standing at 5.0 km, 50 m range" [:br {}] "Total Climbing: 152 m"]]]] [:div {:class "description"} [:p {} "As expected, the 1980 Biathlon relay became a duel between the defending Olympic Champion Soviet Union and East Germany, World Champion in 1978 and 1979. At the first leg, the Soviet Union’s " [:a {:href "/athletes/83536"} "Vladimir Alikin"] " took a 23-second lead over East Germany’s 21-year-old " [:a {:href "/athletes/87673"} "Mathias Jung"] ", who was making his international championship début. France was in third, followed by Austria and Finland, all well behind the two leading teams. At the second leg, " [:a {:href "/athletes/98275"} "Aleksandr Tikhonov"] ", the 33-year old Soviet veteran, already with three Olympic relay gold medals and six World Championships relay gold medals in his pocket, expanded the Soviet lead to almost 1½ minutes over East Germany’s " [:a {:href "/athletes/97520"} "Klaus Siebert"] ", who had to ski two penalty laps. Despite " [:a {:href "/athletes/98475"} "Frank Ullrich"] "’s superb third leg, gaining 47 seconds on the Soviet Union’s " [:a {:href "/athletes/83855"} "Vladimir Barnashov"] ", anchor skier " [:a {:href "/athletes/83572"} "Anatoly Alyabyev"] " had no problems in securing another relay gold medal for the Soviet team, their fourth out of four possible so far at the Olympics. And Tikhonov had been a team-member on all four occasions!"] "\n\n" [:p {} [:a {:href "/athletes/97053"} "Eberhard Rösch"] " secured East Germany’s first Olympic biathlon relay silver medal, having won bronze medals in both 1972 and 1976. The fight for the bronze medal was close. West Germany’s 20-year-old " [:a {:href "/athletes/83647"} "Peter Angerer"] " had a solid third leg for his team, advancing from seventh to third, closely followed by Norway and France. On the anchor leg, " [:a {:href "/athletes/98991"} "Gerd Winkler"] " went away from his contenders and clinched the first ever international relay medal for West Germany."] "\n"] [:table {:class "table table-striped"} [:thead {} [:tr {} [:th {} "Pos"] [:th {} "Competitors"] [:th {} "NOC"] [:th {} "Time"] [:th {} "Misses"] [:th {} "Extra 